    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13664" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποσεύω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>chase away,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Th.</u>
				77
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				9.642
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Agath.
			</span></i>):—
				Pass.
			, <i>run away, flee,</i><i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> only in syncop.aor. 2
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπέσσυτο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					6.390
				</span></i>
			, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπεσσύμεναι θύγατρες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					B.
					10.82
				</span></i>
			: also aor.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπεσσύθην [ν̆</span>] <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				183
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποσνθὲν αἷμα,</span>
			<i>haemorrhage,</i>
			
				v.l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποχυθέν</span>
			 in <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
			</span></i><i>Acut.(Sp.)</i><i><span class="en">
				29
			</span></i>:— 
				Med.
			, =
			
				Act.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπεσσεύοντο γυναῖκας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					1.805
				</span></i>
			.</div>
